[{"order":1,"type":"heading","text":"Handling Multiple Windows and Tabs in Selenium"},{"order":2,"type":"paragraph","text":"Modern web applications frequently open new browser windows or tabs in response to user actions, such as clicking external links, password resets, or viewing documents. Selenium WebDriver provides robust mechanisms to handle these multiple contexts seamlessly using Window Handles and the New Tab API."},{"order":3,"type":"subheading","text":"Understanding Window Handles"},{"order":4,"type":"paragraph","text":"Every browser window or tab opened by WebDriver is assigned a unique alphanumeric identifier known as a window handle. Selenium maintains the focus on the initial window until you explicitly instruct it to switch to a different window handle using the driver.switchTo().window(handle) method."},{"order":5,"type":"subheading","text":"Retrieving and Switching Window Handles"},{"order":6,"type":"paragraph","text":"To interact with multiple windows, you need to retrieve the handle of the current window and the set of all available window handles. Here is a standard approach implemented in Java:"},{"order":7,"type":"code","text":"String mainWindowHandle = driver.getWindowHandle();
System.out.println("Main Window ID: " + mainWindowHandle);

// Trigger action that opens a new tab/window
driver.findElement(By.id("openNewWindowBtn")).click();

// Get all window handles
Set<String> allWindowHandles = driver.getWindowHandles();

for (String handle : allWindowHandles) {
    if (!handle.equals(mainWindowHandle)) {
        driver.switchTo().window(handle);
        break;
    }
}

// Perform actions on the new window
System.out.println("New Window Title: " + driver.getTitle());

// Close the new window and switch back
driver.close();
driver.switchTo().window(mainWindowHandle);"},{"order":8,"type":"subheading","text":"Using the Selenium 4 New Tab and Window API"},{"order":9,"type":"paragraph","text":"Starting with Selenium 4, the framework introduced a dedicated Window type API that allows developers to programmatically open and switch to a brand new tab or window without relying on user UI interactions. This simplifies test setup and execution."},{"order":10,"type":"code","text":"// Open a new tab and switch to it immediately
driver.switchTo().newWindow(WindowType.TAB);
driver.get("https://www.example.com");

// Alternatively, open a completely new browser window
driver.switchTo().newWindow(WindowType.WINDOW);
driver.get("https://www.example.org");"},{"order":11,"type":"subheading","text":"Best Practices for Window Management"},{"order":12,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Always capture the parent window handle before performing actions that spawn new tabs to ensure you can reliably return to the context."},{"order":13,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Use driver.close() to close the currently focused window or tab, and driver.quit() to terminate the entire driver session and close all associated windows."},{"order":14,"type":"bullet_point","text":"Implement explicit waits after switching windows to ensure that elements in the new DOM are fully loaded before interaction."}]
